/-!
# Properties of quasi-coherent modules across `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝓕` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module.  Descent, Proposition 03DX makes
`𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` an equivalence `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪)` for every
`τ ∈ {Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic, fppf}`, and an equivalence `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)`
on the small sites.  Descent, Lemma 05VG says that these equivalences preserve and reflect the
properties of modules of Modules on Sites, Definitions 03DE, 03DL and 03ER:
`𝓕` has `𝒫` if and only if `𝓕^a` has `𝒫` as an `𝒪`-module.  The source's list is: free, finite
free, generated by global sections, generated by `r` global sections, generated by finitely many
global sections, having a global presentation, having a global finite presentation, locally free,
finite locally free, locally generated by sections, locally generated by `r` sections, finite
type, of finite presentation, coherent, flat.

This file states the lemma property by property, each theorem listing every site at once: for
a quasi-coherent `𝓕` and a property `𝒫`, the conjunction of

* `𝒫 𝓕 ↔ 𝒫 𝓕^a` on the big site `(Sch/S)_τ`, for every `τ : AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind`;
* `𝒫 𝓕 ↔ 𝒫 𝓕^a` on the small Zariski site `S_Zar`;
* `𝒫 𝓕 ↔ 𝒫 𝓕^a` on the small étale site `S_étale`;
* `𝒫 𝓕 ↔ 𝒫 𝓕^a` on the small site `S_τ`, for every `τ : AlgebraicGeometry.FlatSiteKind`, that
  is `τ ∈ {smooth, syntomic, fppf}`.

In every case `𝓕^a` is the associated module of Definition 03DU, the functor of 03DX:
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModule`, `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`
and `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.associatedModule`.

## Main results

One theorem per property, all in the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`:

* free (03DE (1)): `isFree_iff_associatedModule`;
* finite free (03DE (2)): `isFiniteFree_iff_associatedModule`;
* generated by global sections (03DE (3)): `isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_associatedModule`;
* generated by `r` global sections (03DE (4)):
  `isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_associatedModule`;
* generated by finitely many global sections (03DE (5)):
  `exists_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_associatedModule`;
* having a global presentation (03DE (6)): `isPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_associatedModule`;
* having a global finite presentation (03DE (7)):
  `isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_associatedModule`;
* finite locally free (03DL (2)): `isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_associatedModule`;
* locally generated by sections (03DL (3)):
  `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_associatedModule`;
* locally generated by `r` sections (03DL (4)): `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_associatedModule`;
* finite type (03DL (5)): `isFiniteType_iff_associatedModule`;
* of finite presentation (03DL (7)): `isFinitePresentation_iff_associatedModule`;
* coherent (03DL (8)), `S` locally Noetherian: `isCoherent_iff_associatedModule`;
* flat (03ER (3)): `isFlat_iff_associatedModule`.

Where each site sits in the theorem `h` for `𝒫` (for `τ : SiteKind`, `κ : FlatSiteKind`):

| `𝒫` | `(Sch/S)_τ`, every `τ` | `S_Zar` | `S_étale` | `S_κ`, `κ` smooth/syntomic/fppf |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| free | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| finite free | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| generated by global sections | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| generated by `r` global sections | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| generated by finitely many global sections | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| having a global presentation | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| having a global finite presentation | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| locally free | excepted | excepted | excepted | excepted |
| finite locally free | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| locally generated by sections | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| locally generated by `r` sections | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| finite type | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| of finite presentation | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |
| coherent, `S` locally Noetherian | not asserted | `h.1` | `h.2` | not asserted |
| flat | `h.1 τ` | `h.2.1` | `h.2.2.1` | `h.2.2.2 κ` |

## Implementation notes

The source excepts two properties: the equivalence holds "except (possibly) when `𝒫` is 'locally
free' or 'coherent'.  If `𝒫` = 'coherent' the equivalence holds for
`QCoh(𝒪_S) → QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)` when `S` is locally Noetherian and `τ` is Zariski or étale."
Accordingly there is no theorem for local freeness, and the coherent theorem is stated for the
two small sites over a locally Noetherian `S` only.

The four kinds of site need three big sites in the sense of Topologies, Definitions 020S, 021L
and 021S: a big fppf site `Bf`, whose underlying category carries the big sites `(Sch/S)_τ` for
every `τ` and the small sites `S_τ` for `τ ∈ {smooth, syntomic, fppf}`; a big étale site `Be`,
carrying `S_étale`; and a big Zariski site `Bz`, carrying `S_Zar`.  Each contains `S`.

Each conjunct is proved site by site, for the global properties of 03DE by full faithfulness of
`𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` on `QCoh(𝒪_S)` together with its preservation of colimits and of the structure sheaf,
and for the local properties through the covering descriptions of 03DN and the descent lemmas
for quasi-coherent modules; the site-by-site statements are cited in the proofs.

